<article class="env-lemma" id="0917">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0917">Lemma <span data-tag="0917">15.57.3</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a ring map. If $I^\bullet $ is a K-injective complex of $A$-modules, then $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ A(B, I^\bullet )$ is a K-injective complex of $B$-modules. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{K(B)}(N^\bullet , \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ A(B, I^\bullet )) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{K(A)}(N^\bullet , I^\bullet )$ by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/08YP" data-tag="08YP">10.14.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>